From 79506632da3407902c37f54ee9759df3ae431123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:14:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sdp-hdmi: add SDP1412 HDMI transmitter probe skeleton
 (patch 0018)

Add DT node and probe-only skeleton for the Samsung SDP1412 (Nike-L)
HDMI transmitter.  All hardware values from firmware dtb0
(T-NKLDEUC 2743.0 dtb.bin, nikel-2G, sha256 0189cc94,
node /soc/hdmi@00590000).

DT node hdmi@590000 in sdp-nikel.dtsi:
  - reg: 7 regions with reg-names matching firmware:
    hdmi-reg (0x590000 0x20000), hdmi-edid-reg (0x970000 0x5a0),
    hdmi-common-reg (0x5c0000 0xffff), hdmi-esm-reg (0x5b0000 0x8000),
    hdmi-dsc-musem-reg (0x5b8000 0x300),
    hdmi-dsc-museo-reg (0x20898000 0x300),
    hdmi-fec-museo-reg (0x20898800 0x300)
  - interrupts: 8 IRQs (GIC SPI 88, 89, 90, 104, 105, 106, 109, 93),
    exact order from firmware <0x0 0x5[89a] 0x0> etc.
  - clocks: TBD (hdmi_pclk, hdmi_sysclk, hdmi_modclk indices unknown)
  - status = "disabled"

drivers/gpu/drm/sdp-hdmi/sdp_hdmi.c:
  - Maps 7 MMIO regions, requests 8 IRQs with IRQF_NO_AUTOEN
    (IRQ handler is a stub until register layout is known)
  - Returns 0 from probe

No GPL driver source was found for samsung,sdp-hdmi.
No register offsets invented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HFSjk2L7MPX5r9CMRGhqwJ
